				</html>
			</example>
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-message size="small" class="site-not-ported">Not ported: Gradual Changes, per-pixel <code>onPassing</> updates (checks happen at crossings only). For a style that follows the scroll, use CSS scroll-driven animations (<code>animation-timeline: view()</>), which need no script at all.</>
			<ui-message size="small" class="site-not-ported">Not ported: Fixing Content To Viewport (<code>type: 'fixed'</>) -- that's <a href="/components/ui/ui-sticky.html"><code>&lt;ui-sticky&gt;</></>, on CSS <code>position: sticky</> with no placeholder element.</>
		</>

		<section label="Infinite Scroll" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="As an alternative to pagination, listen for `ui-bottom-in-view` with `once=\"false\"` and load more content when the bottom of a container is reached. Here the page's script adds three items each time, up to twelve.">
				<visibility id="visibility-infinite" once="false">
					<segment>
						<header level="3" align="center">Infinite Scroll Example</header>
						<list id="visibility-infinite-list" divided spacing="lg">
							<item>Item 1</item>
							<item>Item 2</item>
							<item>Item 3</item>
						</list>
						<loader id="visibility-infinite-loader" inline align="center" size="small"/>
					</segment>
				</visibility>
			</example>
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
